# Campaign Spec Schema

**File:** `campaign.yaml`

This document defines the structure and rules for `campaign.yaml` files used by the Meta Ads CLI Harness.

The schema is designed to be:
- Human readable
- Version controllable in git
- Easy to customize per client

## File Location

Each campaign gets its own folder. Place `campaign.yaml` inside it:
clients/<client-name>/campaigns/<campaign-slug>/campaign.yaml
text## Schema Structure

### Required Top-Level Field

```yaml
ad_account_id: act_XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
Campaign Section
YAMLcampaign:
  name: "YYYYMMDD_Meta_Web_FunnelStage_Geo_OptEvent_BudgetType_Theme"
  objective: OUTCOME_SALES
  daily_budget_cents: 5000
Valid objective values:

OUTCOME_SALES
OUTCOME_TRAFFIC
OUTCOME_AWARENESS

Ad Set Section
YAMLadset:
  name: "YYYYMMDD_Meta_Web_FunnelStage_Geo_OptEvent_BudgetType_Theme_V1"
  optimization_goal: OFFSITE_CONVERSIONS
  billing_event: IMPRESSIONS
  countries: [US]
  pixel_id: "123456789012345"
  custom_event_type: Purchase
Common optimization_goal values:

OFFSITE_CONVERSIONS
LINK_CLICKS
IMPRESSIONS

Note: pixel_id and custom_event_type are only required when using OFFSITE_CONVERSIONS.
Creatives Section
YAMLcreatives:
  - name: "CreativeName_V1"
    image: images/creative-v1.jpg
    page_id: "123456789012345"
    body: >
      Your primary ad text goes here.
    title: "Your Headline"
    link_url: "https://yourdomain.com/landing-page"
    cta: LEARN_MORE
Supported cta values:
LEARN_MORE, SIGN_UP, SHOP_NOW, BUY_NOW, CONTACT_US, DOWNLOAD, APPLY_NOW, GET_OFFER, SUBSCRIBE, WATCH_MORE
Image/Video Rules:

Use either image: or video: (not both)
Image files go in the images/ folder (minimum 1080×1080)
Video files go in the videos/ folder

Ads Section
YAMLads:
  - name: "AdName_V1"
    creative_ref: "CreativeName_V1"
Important: The creative_ref value must exactly match the name of a creative defined above.
Complete Minimal Example
YAMLad_account_id: act_XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX

campaign:
  name: "20250611_Meta_Web_Prospecting_US_Purchase_Broad_Test"
  objective: OUTCOME_SALES
  daily_budget_cents: 5000

adset:
  name: "20250611_Meta_Web_Prospecting_US_Purchase_Broad_Test_V1"
  optimization_goal: OFFSITE_CONVERSIONS
  billing_event: IMPRESSIONS
  countries: [US]
  pixel_id: "123456789012345"
  custom_event_type: Purchase

creatives:
  - name: "Feed_V1"
    image: images/feed-v1.jpg
    page_id: "123456789012345"
    body: >
      Your main ad copy goes here. Keep it concise.
    title: "Compelling Headline"
    link_url: "https://yourdomain.com/offer"
    cta: LEARN_MORE

ads:
  - name: "Ad_V1"
    creative_ref: "Feed_V1"
Rules & Best Practices

All campaigns, ad sets, and ads are created in PAUSED status by default.
Use clear, consistent naming conventions in the name fields.
Store repeated values (pixel ID, page ID, ad account ID) in your client’s .env file when possible.
Tracking parameters are automatically added by the harness.
Do not delete or modify state.json or log files manually unless you know what you’re doing.

Notes for Companies Using This Toolkit
Replace all placeholder values with your own Meta account details.
Common values (pixel ID, page ID, etc.) can be stored in clients/<your-client>/.env to avoid repetition across campaigns.
